{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0423","billNumberShort":"H.B. 423","billNumberLong":"HB0423S05","fileNumber":"2026FL0155","shortTitle":"Hit and Run and DUI Offense Amendments","currentSubVersion":"5","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"ELIASS","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Eliason, Steve","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"WEILET","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Weiler, Todd","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill increases the penalty for leaving the scene of an accident and modifies deadlines for an administrative driver license hearing following an individual's arrest for driving under the influence.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>increases penalties for convictions of leaving the scene of an accident with property damage or injury if the operator has been previously convicted of:<hr><ltbullet1>the same offense; or<hr><ltbullet1>driving under the influence;<hr><ltbullet>creates a mitigation against an enhanced offense for an individual who obtains a negative chemical test;<hr><ltbullet>allows the Driver License Division to request a peace officer's presence for a driver license suspension hearing;<hr><ltbullet>adds that a Driver License Division hearing for a driving under the influence arrest cannot be dismissed solely due to a peace officer's failure to appear; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Riley Williams","fiscalAnalyst":"Gary R. Syphus","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/24/2026","trackingID":"NXALUQUPXM","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-29 09:25:45.923","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Re